  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\npackage:\n  name: cnchash\n  version: 2.0.0\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/Chuan1937/CNCHASH/archive/refs/tags/v2.0.0.tar.gz\n  sha256: 09475d9cb617f8d505723a36cbd8c8114dd9c4831b5e871acd7b4dca9bcca83b\n\nbuild:\n  # Windows is skipped for now: the Python front-end hard-codes the\n  # libhashhp.so search path and the flang/OpenMP toolchain needs\n  # validation. Linux and macOS are built.\n  number: 0\n  skip: win\n  script:\n    - cmake -S . -B build-conda -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DCNCHASH_BUILD_TESTS=OFF ${CMAKE_ARGS}\n    - cmake --build build-conda -j ${CPU_COUNT}\n    - ${PYTHON} -m pip install . --no-deps --no-build-isolation -vv\n    - |\n      NATIVE_LIB=build-conda/libhashhp${SHLIB_EXT}\n      if [ ! -f ${NATIVE_LIB} ]; then\n        echo \"libhashhp shared library not found in build-conda\" >&2\n        exit 1\n      fi\n    - mkdir -p ${SP_DIR}/cnchash/lib\n    - cp ${NATIVE_LIB} ${SP_DIR}/cnchash/lib/libhashhp.so\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler('fortran') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - cmake >=3.16\n    - make\n  host:\n    - python\n    - pip\n    - setuptools >=61\n    - wheel\n    - if: linux\n      then: libgomp\n    - if: osx\n      then: llvm-openmp\n  run:\n    - python\n    - numpy >=1.20\n    # OpenMP runtime: the compiler run_exports no longer add it, so\n    # declare it explicitly on both platforms.\n    - if: linux\n      then: libgomp\n    - if: osx\n      then: llvm-openmp\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - cnchash\n  - script: run_test.py\n\nabout:\n  license: BSD-3-Clause\n  license_file: LICENSE\n  summary: >-\n    High-performance HASH earthquake focal-mechanism solver with a Modern\n    Fortran/OpenMP native backend and a clean Python front-end.\n  description: >-\n    CNCHASH determines earthquake focal mechanisms from P-wave polarities\n    and optional S/P amplitude ratios using the HASH algorithm (Hardebeck\n    and Shearer, 2002, 2003). All computation runs in a Modern\n    Fortran/OpenMP core (libhashhp); the Python layer handles data, file\n    formats, and the API.\n  homepage: https://github.com/Chuan1937/CNCHASH\n  repository: https://github.com/Chuan1937/CNCHASH\n  documentation: https://chuan1937.github.io/CNCHASH/\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - Chuan1937\n",
